# LightGBM writes a model as a .txt file, but it is not text in the line-ending sense. Git on
# Windows treats .txt as text by default and rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which corrupts it:
# a fresh clone then fails to load the model at all, with
#
#     [LightGBM] [Fatal] Model format error, expect a tree here
#
# and the submission cannot be reproduced. Found by cloning this repository into an empty
# directory and running the pipeline from the clone, which is the only way to find it -- the
# working copy the models were written in is fine, and so is the blob in the repository. Only
# the checkout is wrong, so nothing here is visible until somebody else clones it.
#
# These are the two files the whole reproduction depends on.
submit/models/*.txt -text
submit/models/*.npz binary

# Everything else is genuinely text and may be normalised as usual.
*.py text
*.md text
*.csv text
*.json text
*.html text
